    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson** headlining the lineup as the clear must-start options. **Gunnar Henderson** (76.16) leverages a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta, bolstered by a 6% boost for his #3 order slot and a critical 2% efficiency gain from Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability window for stolen base accumulation. **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) offers the highest ceiling of the day, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Bradford (5.29 xERA). His 19% SP skill boost makes him a prime candidate for a multi-hit performance, especially given the +10% park factor advantage working in his favor. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (69.57) rounds out the top tier, benefiting significantly from a dynamic platoon edge against Bibee.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo** (43.08). While he projected as a viable utility candidate, he narrowly missed the cut due to a negative platoon split against Peralta and a lower spot in the order compared to the high-volume opportunities for **Dominic Smith** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are opting to sacrifice a fraction of power for the structural stability of the current lineup. Managerial oversight remains directed toward our elite talent; specifically, we are tracking **Kyle Tucker** (51.47) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (56.52), both of whom are facing challenging arms in Henderson and Cease. Despite the high caliber of these opposing pitchers, their historical efficiency and order placement justify the start, though we have flagged their scores as \"Marginal\" compared to our primary anchors.\n\nRisk mitigation is paramount today as several players are navigating unfavorable platoon alignments. **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.15) faces a stiff 15% penalty due to his dynamic platoon setup, but we are keeping him active strictly for the stolen base upside against Irvin, who is susceptible to high-speed runners. As the season winds down, we are monitoring all game caps carefully; with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** confirmed on the IL, our roster depth\u2014including **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Liam Hicks**\u2014remains on standby should the weather or late lineup shifts necessitate a pivot from our current rotation.",
